{
 "description": "U1/R5: hotkey-to-first-frame p99 < 200 ms and p50 < 80 ms over 50 triggers (hidden between each), and the panel opens on the display under the cursor",
 "requirement": "R5 (GPUI Phase 0), U1",
 "notes": [
  "Each trigger is a block (a focus theft re-runs it once, see probes/README.md), so counts are checked with ge: a re-run may add a sample.",
  "Generated: 50 x (trigger_hotkey open, wait for the sample, trigger_hotkey again to toggle it hidden), cycling capture/browser/settings. Each show is a fresh window.",
  "t0 = the shell receives the hotkey (shell::handle_event, where trigger_hotkey and a real Carbon event both enter); t1 = after the first platform frame's present returned (shell/panel.rs arm_first_frame explains the hook).",
  "No a11y call before the loop: activating a window's AccessKit tree makes GPUI build it on every frame for that window's life.",
  "summary.* uses nearest-rank percentiles: p99 of 50 samples is the slowest one.",
  "Single-display placement only; panel-multidisplay.json holds the >= 2 display assertions (ENV-BLOCKED on one display), kept apart so this scenario exits 0 on a one-display Mac."
 ],
 "steps": [
  {
   "name": "nothing timed yet",
   "call": "metrics",
   "expect": {
    "summary.hotkey_to_first_frame.count": 0,
    "capacity": {
     "ge": 50
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "cursor on the main display",
   "warp_cursor": 0
  },
  {
   "name": "trigger 1/50 opens",
   "block": "trigger-1",
   "call": "trigger_hotkey",
   "args": {
    "action": "capture"
   },
   "expect": {
    "route": "capture",
    "shell.visible": true
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "trigger 1/50 timed",
   "block": "trigger-1",
   "call": "metrics",
   "retry_ms": 3000,
   "expect": {
    "summary.hotkey_to_first_frame.count": {
     "ge": 1
    }
   }
  },
  {
   "name": "trigger 1/50 hides",
   "block": "trigger-1",
   "call": "trigger_hotkey",
   "args": {
    "action": "capture"
   },
   "expect": {
    "route": null,
    "shell.visible": false
   }
  },
  {
